      <p class="eyebrow">Benzene</p>
      <h2 id="benz-h">Benzene exposure is not just a refinery problem anymore</h2>
      <p>Louisiana's petrochemical corridor has exposed generations of workers to benzene — a known human carcinogen linked to acute myeloid leukemia (AML), myelodysplastic syndromes (MDS), and other blood cancers. Today, benzene is also turning up in consumer products, from aerosol sunscreens to antifungal sprays.</p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Refinery, chemical plant, pipeline and terminal workers</li>
        <li>Mechanics, painters and anyone working with solvents or fuels</li>
        <li>Families living near plants along the river corridor</li>
        <li>People who used recalled benzene-contaminated products</li>
      </ul>
